#: ../../../data2/home/huanghaoyu/AgentSociety/agentsociety2/agentsociety/packages/agentsociety2/docs/api/http.rst:86
msgid ""
"实验与回放接口需要 ``workspace_path`` 查询参数，值为后端可访问的研究工作区绝对路径。通过扩展操作时由扩展传入；手动调用时按 Swagger "
"填写。``WORKSPACE_PATH`` 配置后端允许访问的工作区范围，具体约束见 :doc:`/installation`。工作区目录及实验产物约定见 :doc:`/user_guide"
"/research-project` 与 :doc:`/results`。"
msgstr ""
"Experiment and replay endpoints require a ``workspace_path`` query parameter containing an "
"absolute research workspace path accessible to the backend. The extension supplies it "
"automatically; for manual requests, enter it as shown in Swagger. ``WORKSPACE_PATH`` configures "
"the workspace scope accessible to the backend; see :doc:`/installation` for the constraints. See "
":doc:`/user_guide/research-project` and :doc:`/results` for workspace directories and experiment "
"artifacts."

#: ../../../data2/home/huanghaoyu/AgentSociety/agentsociety2/agentsociety/packages/agentsociety2/docs/api/http.rst:88
msgid ""
"后端默认监听回环地址，当前没有内置用户登录认证。LLM 供应商的 API Key 用于调用模型，不是此后端的访问凭据。需要远程访问时，应配置访问认证的反向代理，并按 "
":doc:`/installation` 设置可信主机与浏览器来源。"
msgstr ""
"The backend listens on the loopback address by default and currently has no built-in user "
"authentication. An LLM provider API key authenticates model calls, not access to this backend. "
"For remote access, configure a reverse proxy with authentication and set trusted hosts and "
"browser origins as described in :doc:`/installation`."

#: ../../../data2/home/huanghaoyu/AgentSociety/agentsociety2/agentsociety/packages/agentsociety2/docs/api/http.rst:90
msgid ""
"无法访问 ``/docs`` 时，先确认后端地址和 ``/health``；页面打开后界面仍空白时，检查浏览器能否加载 Swagger 的外部静态资源。框架提供的文档方式见 `FastAPI "
"自动文档说明 <https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/features/#automatic-docs>`_。"
msgstr ""
"If ``/docs`` is unreachable, check the backend address and ``/health`` first. If the page opens "
"but remains blank, check whether the browser can load the external Swagger assets. See `FastAPI "
"automatic documentation <https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/features/#automatic-docs>`_ for the "
"documentation interfaces provided by the framework."

